  "review_notes": [
    "Every1064B original and2684B organized byte read individually. The complete structure retains S:AdelicSpectralSheaf, i/j:Place, two defaulted stored places, both stored spectra, a genuine SpectrumMorphism between those spectra, an unproved local-factor Prop and a supplied boundary Prop proof.",
    "sourcePlace:=i and targetPlace:=j are field defaults, not proof fields imposing equality: callers may supply other stored places. No equation links sourceSpectrum/targetSpectrum/morphism to S.sheaf, i or j. SpectrumMorphism itself really stores a carrier map but has an independent chosen stability-preservation Prop, not a commuting diagram law.",
    "restriction_compatible_with_boundary genuinely projects the stored proof under every original S,i,j,rho premise. No actual local-factor/boundary comparison formula or presheaf identity/composition law is introduced. Preserve the whole mixed same-file provider and theorem in exact archive; no narrowed type, self-import or historical provider substitution."
  ],
